across 18 services.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Contain vulnerable surfaces and build a compatibility matrix for old and new serialization behavior.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Run contract, corpus, differential, and staged integration tests across service-version combinations.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select rollout order by exposure reduction, compatibility evidence, and ease of rollback.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Security and platform owners approve exceptions, sequencing, and residual vulnerability risk.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Security owner halts rollout on incompatible payloads, integrity loss, or unbounded rollback risk.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record payload edge cases, service compatibility boundaries, and dependency-upgrade playbook improvements.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe06\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"The pipeline has demonstrated silent loss without reconciliation, ownership, or a trusted completeness signal.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Quarantine affected outputs and add input-output counts with explicit loss detection.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Trace record paths, compare independent counts and samples, identify drop points, and generate ownership candidates.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Fund fixes that restore observable completeness and isolate loss mechanisms before optimization.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Operations owner assigns accountability and decides treatment of already-delivered incomplete outputs.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Owner stops downstream publication when reconciliation fails or loss remains undetected.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Create an ownership map, reconciliation invariant, incident taxonomy, and recurring loss monitor.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe07\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Existing callers depend on ambiguous behavior while production defects show the ambiguity is costly.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Characterize current call patterns and publish an explicit semantic contract.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Mine call sites, generate compatibility wrappers, add misuse tests, and compare old-versus-new outputs.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Adopt a new unambiguous method while preserving the old path until observed migration evidence is sufficient.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"SDK owner chooses naming, deprecation timing, and acceptable behavior changes.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Owner pauses deprecation when telemetry or support evidence shows unresolved caller dependency.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Capture ambiguity patterns, migration friction, and contract tests for future SDK changes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n01\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Thirty mechanisms and 400 overlapping papers exceed available attention, with uncertain evidence independence.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Cluster mechanisms by failure mode and select three experiments with distinct predictions and cheap reversibility.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Deduplicate papers, extract conditions and outcomes, map evidence dependencies, and generate prediction tables.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose experiments maximizing mechanism diversity, information gain, and recoverability under budget.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Research lead judges whether evidence quality warrants advancing, merging, or abandoning a mechanism.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Lead stops an experiment when its result cannot distinguish mechanisms or conditions are not controlled.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Maintain a mechanism-evidence graph and update priors only from independent, discriminating results.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n02\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Computational support may be irrelevant if the conjecture's graph class is misstated.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Formalize the claimed graph class and test whether all examples satisfy it.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Check definitions, generate counterexamples, verify examples independently, and search boundary cases.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Advance only conjecture variants whose domain and invariant survive definition and counterexample tests.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Mathematician decides the corrected statement and whether computation merits proof effort.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Mathematician abandons a formulation after a valid counterexample or unresolved class ambiguity.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record rejected formulations, minimal counterexamples, and verified computational invariants.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n03\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Only two reversible tests are affordable and competitor adaptation can confound durable effects.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Define the free-tier hypothesis, guardrails, and leading indicators before exposing users.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Simulate scenarios, segment cohorts, instrument conversion and support costs, and run two staged tests.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose tests that separate acquisition, conversion, cannibalization, and competitor-response hypotheses.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Founder decides whether observed evidence justifies continuation despite strategic uncertainty.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Founder stops a test on margin erosion, abuse, service degradation, or weak discriminating signal.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Document elasticities, cohort effects, competitor responses, and the conditions for a future test.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n04\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Validation, data practices, retention, appeal, and compliance status are unknown.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Inventory unknowns and pause deployment claims until accountable owners verify them.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Generate a requirements matrix, trace data flows, test validation procedures, and draft conditional notice language.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select only claims and processes supported by verified controls; leave unknowns explicitly unresolved.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Legal and HR owners approve scope, disclosures, retention, and appeal commitments.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Compliance owner blocks publication or use when a required safeguard lacks evidence.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Maintain a control register linking each notice claim to validation and governance evidence.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n05\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"One instructor must individualize practice and assess 90 mixed-level engineers reliably.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Baseline proficiency and group learners by observable technical-English needs.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Generate adaptive exercises, feedback variants, scoring rubrics, and progress summaries.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Allocate attention to interventions with measured improvement, transfer, and assessment reliability.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Instructor reviews borderline cases, calibrates scoring, and adjusts learner pathways.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Instructor stops an exercise or assessment when it produces unreliable scores or misleading feedback.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain error patterns, item performance, rubric calibration, and effective practice sequences.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n06\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Arrivals and downtime vary, urgent samples cannot be delayed, and capacity is unknown.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Map current queues and reserve explicit priority paths without assuming throughput.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Model scenarios, forecast queues from observed arrivals, simulate downtime, and suggest dispatch rules.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose scheduling rules that protect urgent turnaround while remaining reversible under observed conditions.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Lab operations lead sets priority policy and interprets real-time exceptions.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Lead suspends a rule when urgent delay, safety risk, or queue instability exceeds the agreed threshold.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Collect arrival, service, downtime, and exception data to improve the scheduling model.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n07\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"The system must work across four languages and visual impairments in a hospital context.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Map journeys and accessibility failure modes with representative users.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Generate multilingual sign variants, route simulations, contrast checks, and tactile/audio alternatives.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select concepts by tested comprehension, localization accuracy, accessibility, and reversible deployment cost.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Design and clinical stakeholders approve terminology, safety implications, and pilot locations.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Stakeholders halt a concept when users misroute, miss critical information, or encounter accessibility barriers.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record user errors, language-specific ambiguity, accessibility findings, and site-specific constraints.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n08\",\n    \"domain\": \"writing\",\n    \"task\": \"Synthesize 300 interview transcripts into a board decision without erasing minority evidence or exposing identities.\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"The synthesis must support a decision while preserving minority signals and protecting participant identity.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Create an anonymized evidence index with provenance, prevalence, and sensitivity labels.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Cluster themes, detect contradictions, quantify representation, redact identifiers, and draft competing decision frames.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select recommendations supported by evidence strength and decision relevance, with minority exceptions visible.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Board sponsor decides tradeoffs and reviews sensitive or consequential interpretations.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Research owner blocks publication when re-identification risk or unsupported synthesis remains.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Preserve the coded corpus, dissent log, provenance links, and privacy lessons.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n09\",\n    \"domain\": \"research\",\n    \"task\": \"Map a fast-moving technical field while detecting duplicated datasets, benchmark leakage, and contradictory results.\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Rapid publication and shared data can make apparent evidence non-independent or invalid.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Build a provenance-first map of datasets, benchmarks, claims, and replication relationships.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Deduplicate sources, trace dataset lineage, test leakage indicators, and reconcile contradictory results.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Rank claims by independent support, leakage risk, recency, and reproducibility.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Field lead decides which uncertainties merit replication or exclusion from strategic conclusions.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Lead withholds a claim when provenance is unresolved or benchmark validity is compromised.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Maintain lineage graphs, contradiction records, leakage tests, and update timestamps.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n10\",\n    \"domain\": \"simulation\",\n    \"task\": \"Assess whether cooperation survives across uncertain evolutionary-game payoffs without treating authored ranges as empirical probabilities.\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Payoff ranges express uncertainty or authorship, not validated probability distributions.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Separate empirical inputs, scenario ranges, and model assumptions before running simulations.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Run sensitivity, adversarial, and parameter-sweep simulations with outcome envelopes rather than false probabilities.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select cooperation mechanisms robust across plausible scenarios, not merely favorable sampled draws.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Model owner judges scenario plausibility and whether results support a bounded conclusion.